{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_lugdywjc7lohaggggyi7tk3wqxt5qzhulqesauc2odor3tebao7a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01YBGgLi4T83NFa6q7r85uAS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-3rdGDT/translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (Phase A / gate for Phase B)\n\nMechanically derived from the branches `c_src/src/lib.c` actually takes.\n\n## Public surface\n\n`c_src/include/lib.h` declares exactly one function:\n\n```c\nint pinflate(void *in, int in_bytes, void *out, int out_bytes);\n```\n\nThere is **no** options struct, no init/reset call and no `#ifdef`-gated\nfeature.  Everything the library does is selected by the *content* of the input\nbit stream and by the *shape* of the two buffers.  In addition, seven **mutable\nglobals** are exported (`cp_fixed_table`, `cp_permutation_order`,\n`cp_len_extra_bits`, `cp_len_base`, `cp_dist_extra_bits`, `cp_dist_base`,\n`cp_error_reason`) — these are genuine run-time \"options\" an external caller can\nset, and the code reads them on every call, so they are treated as an axis.\n\nThere is **no binary/driver target** in `CMakeLists.txt` (only\n`add_library(... SHARED)`), so the \"compare stdout of two executables\" part of\nPhase B does not apply.  Instead the fuzz sweep (`tests/fuzz_sweep.rs`) runs\nboth libraries inside re-executed child processes and compares their full\nstdout/stderr/exit-status transcripts byte-for-byte, which covers the same\nground.\n\n## Axes the C code branches on\n\n| axis | values the code distinguishes | where |\n|------|-------------------------------|-------|\n| `BTYPE` | `0` stored, `1` fixed Huffman, `2` dynamic Huffman, `3` reserved(error) | `switch (btype)` lib.c:339 |\n| `BFINAL` | last block / more blocks (`do … while (!bfinal)`) → 1 block vs. many | lib.c:337,371 |\n| block sequence | mixes of stored+fixed+dynamic in one stream | lib.c:336-371 |\n| `in` alignment | `first_bytes = align4(in) - in` ∈ {0,1,2,3}: prologue byte-by-byte load vs. straight word load | lib.c:320-325 |\n| `in_bytes` mod 4 | `last_bytes` ∈ {0,1,2,3}: `final_word_available` 0 or 1 → different `cp_peak_bits` tail path | lib.c:323,326-329 |\n| `in_bytes` size | tiny (`< 4`, so `word_count == 0` and *everything* comes from `first_bytes`/`final_word`), small, large (many word loads) | lib.c:322 |\n| `cp_build` `s` argument | non-NULL (fills the 512-entry `lookup` table *and* the sorted tree) vs. NULL (tree only). Called both ways: `lit` with `s`, `dst`/`len` with `0` | lib.c:139-169, 200-201, 229, 251-252 |\n| code length ≤ 9 vs > 9 | `if (s && len <= 9)` — the `lookup` fast path is only populated for short codes; a tree with 10..15-bit codes takes the other branch | lib.c:158 |\n| `cp_decode` `lo` result | `lo > 0` (normal) vs `lo == 0` (`tree[-1]`, aliased struct member) | lib.c:208-215 |\n| symbol class in `cp_block` | `< 256` literal, `== 256` end-of-block, `> 256` length/distance | lib.c:258,270,307 |\n| `backwards_distance` | `== 1` (`memset` fast path) vs `!= 1` (byte copy loop); and overlapping (`distance < length`) vs non-overlapping | lib.c:299-306 |\n| length symbol | 257..264 (0 extra bits), 265..284 (1..5 extra bits), 285 (`len_base` 258, 0 extra), 286/287 (`len_base == 0` → length 0) | `cp_len_extra_bits`/`cp_len_base`, lib.c:272-273 |\n| distance symbol | 0..3 (0 extra bits), 4..29 (1..13 extra bits), 30/31 (`dist_base == 0` → distance 0 ⇒ `out - 0 >= begin` passes, `memset`-not-taken byte loop over itself) | lib.c:274-277 |\n| code-length symbol | 0..15 literal length, `16` copy-previous (+2 bits), `17` short zero run (+3 bits), `18` long zero run (+7 bits) | `switch (sym)` lib.c:233-249 |\n| `HLIT`/`HDIST`/`HCLEN` | `nlit` 257..288, `ndst` 1..32, `nlen` 4..19 — boundary values each | lib.c:224-226 |\n| stored `LEN` | `0`, `1`, large; and `LEN` vs remaining input (`bits_left/8 <= LEN`) | lib.c:173-193 |\n| `out_bytes` | exactly the decoded size, larger, `0`, smaller than needed | lib.c:260,288,332 |\n| globals | pristine vs. caller-modified (`cp_error_reason` pre-set, `cp_fixed_table` perturbed) | lib.c:40-70 |\n\n## Rows (combinations tested)\n\nEvery row is run with **many randomized inputs** (fixed seed, deterministic\nxorshift PRNG in `tests/common/mod.rs`) and, unless stated otherwise, is\nadditionally crossed with the 16 `(in-alignment × in_bytes mod 4)` combinations\nby the helper `run_all_alignments`, which copies the same stream into buffers at\noffsets 0..3 of a 4-aligned allocation and pads with 0..3 trailing bytes.\n\nLegend for the last column: `[x]` = passes for both libraries.\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [x] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| 1 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=0 stored, BFINAL=1, `LEN` = remaining input, random payload, sizes 0..4096 | [x] |\n| 2 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=0 stored, `LEN == 0` (empty stored block) | [x] |\n| 3 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=0 stored, `LEN == 1` | [x] |\n| 4 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=0 stored, `in` misaligned 0/1/2/3 × `in_bytes % 4` = 0/1/2/3 (16 combinations, exercises `first_bytes` prologue + `final_word` tail) | [x] |\n| 5 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, literals only, `< 256` symbols, random bytes, lengths 1..8192 (drives `cp_build(s,…)` lookup path and `cp_decode` on the 288-symbol tree) | [x] |\n| 6 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, single-literal (shortest possible non-empty stream) | [x] |\n| 7 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, empty (immediate end-of-block symbol 256), `out_bytes = 0` | [x] |\n| 8 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, length/distance pairs with `distance == 1` (`memset` fast path), length 3..258 | [x] |\n| 9 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, `distance < length` (self-overlapping byte-copy loop) | [x] |\n| 10 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, `distance > length` (non-overlapping copy) | [x] |\n| 11 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, every length symbol 257..285 at least once (all `cp_len_extra_bits` classes incl. 0-extra and 5-extra and the 258 special) | [x] |\n| 12 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, every distance symbol 0..29 at least once (all `cp_dist_extra_bits` classes, distances 1..32768 clamped to buffer) | [x] |\n| 13 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=1 fixed, maximum length 258 with maximum distance available | [x] |\n| 14 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, `HLIT`/`HDIST`/`HCLEN` at their minimum (`nlit=257`, `ndst=1`, `nlen=4`) | [x] |\n| 15 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, `HLIT`/`HDIST`/`HCLEN` at their maximum (`nlit=288`, `ndst=32`, `nlen=19`) | [x] |\n| 16 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, code-length stream using symbol `16` (copy-previous run) | [x] |\n| 17 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, code-length stream using symbol `17` (short zero run) | [x] |\n| 18 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, code-length stream using symbol `18` (long zero run, 11..138) | [x] |\n| 19 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, tree containing codes **longer than 9 bits** (skips the `lookup` fast path in `cp_build`) — forced by a highly skewed literal frequency distribution | [x] |\n| 20 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, tree whose codes are all ≤ 9 bits | [x] |\n| 21 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, literals only | [x] |\n| 22 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic, literals + matches (both `cp_decode` trees, `dst` built with `s == NULL`) | [x] |\n| 23 | `pinflate` | BTYPE=2 dynamic produced by a real zlib-class encoder (`flate2`, all compression levels 0..9) over random and highly-repetitive data, 0..65536 bytes | [x] |\n| 24 | `pinflate` | multi-block: stored → fixed → dynamic, `BFINAL` only on the last (`count` loop iterates) | [x] |\n| 25 | `pinflate` | multi-block: 2..8 fixed blocks, back-references crossing block boundaries | [x] |\n| 26 | `pinflate` | multi-block: dynamic blocks with *different* trees, so `cp_build` is re-run and `lookup` is re-zeroed | [x] |\n| 27 | `pinflate` | `out_bytes` exactly equal to the decoded size (tightest passing bound for