{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6prqbjkevlpclyg6awdf4rgnsfd4wer2d2udh26an75g276jjl4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01DnfokkC44jk2VBURfybAfV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/common/mod.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''/// Transcript from ONE library only'''\nnew='''/// Whether `out == NULL` cases may be included in a sweep.\n///\n/// Passing `out == NULL` to a stream that emits a literal makes *both*\n/// libraries dereference a null pointer.  The release `.so` and the C `.so`\n/// both take `SIGSEGV`; a **debug**-profile Rust cdylib instead traps the\n/// dereference with its own \"null pointer dereference occurred\" check and\n/// aborts, so the two die from different signals.  That is a property of the\n/// Rust *debug profile*, not of the translation, so `check_features.sh` sets\n/// `PINFLATE_SKIP_NULL_OUT=1` when it exercises the debug cdylib.  The\n/// null-`out` cases that do **not** dereference (`g03_null_out_empty_block`)\n/// still run in every configuration.\npub fn null_out_allowed() -> bool {\n    std::env::var(\"PINFLATE_SKIP_NULL_OUT\").is_err()\n}\n\n/// Transcript from ONE library only'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/fuzz_sweep.rs'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''        if rng.below(12) == 0 {\n            c = c.null_out();\n        }'''\nnew='''        if rng.below(12) == 0 && null_out_allowed() {\n            c = c.null_out();\n        }'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='check_features.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace('    PINFLATE_RUST_SO=\"$dbg\" cargo test --offline -- --test-threads=4',\n            '    PINFLATE_RUST_SO=\"$dbg\" PINFLATE_SKIP_NULL_OUT=1 cargo test --offline -- --test-threads=4')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ntimeout 200 cargo build --offline --tests 2>&1 | tail -2\ntimeout 500 env PINFLATE_RUST_SO=\"$(pwd)/target/debug/libpinflate_lib.so\" PINFLATE_SKIP_NULL_OUT=1 cargo test --offline -- --test-threads=4 2>&1 | grep -E \"test result|DIVERGENCE|^C   |^Rust:|^case:\" | head -20","description":"Gate null-out cases and rerun debug-cdylib suite","timeout":595000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1248,"cache_read_input_tokens":281255,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1248,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b11a9639-5121-4054-9400-a5599ce5e3a1","uuid":"8e4ca29c-7220-46b1-afa3-7dba79e73a73","timestamp":"2026-09-05T11:20:07.261Z"}
