{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01Kb7SFD5WN57zzxDoV26xRa","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-3rdGDT/translation/SYMBOLS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b11a9639-5121-4054-9400-a5599ce5e3a1","uuid":"76a8a8c5-4288-4f4d-a188-67f0d49ec7e4","timestamp":"2026-09-05T11:27:06.622Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-3rdGDT/translation/SYMBOLS.md","oldString":"Regenerate / diff with:\n\n```sh\n./check_symbols.sh\n```","newString":"Regenerate / diff with:\n\n```sh\n./check_symbols.sh\n```\n\n**Status: the symbol diff (C → Rust) is EMPTY.**  8 symbols exported by the C\n`.so`, all 8 exported by the Rust `.so` under the same names, all 8 resolvable\nthrough `dlsym`, all data symbols the same size.  Verified for the release\ncdylib, for `--no-default-features`, and for the debug cdylib\n(`./check_features.sh`).  Enforced by `tests/symbols.rs` (4 tests) as well as by\n`check_symbols.sh`.","originalFile":"# SYMBOLS.md — public symbol parity (Phase A / Phase D)\n\nSource of truth: `nm -D --defined-only` on the C shared library\n`c_src/build/libharvest-work-3rdGDT.so` (built by CMake, no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`,\ni.e. `-O0` **with `assert()` live** — the `.so` has an undefined reference to\n`__assert_fail`).\n\nRust shared library: `translation/target/release/libpinflate_lib.so`\n(`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`).\n\nRegenerate / diff with:\n\n```sh\n./check_symbols.sh\n```\n\n## Exported (defined) symbols\n\n| # | symbol | C type | Rust definition | present in Rust `.so` |\n|---|--------|--------|-----------------|-----------------------|\n| 1 | `pinflate`             | `T` (text)  | `#[no_mangle] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn pinflate` | yes |\n| 2 | `cp_error_reason`      | `B` (bss)   | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_error_reason: *const c_char` | yes |\n| 3 | `cp_fixed_table`       | `D` (data)  | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_fixed_table: [u8; 320]` | yes |\n| 4 | `cp_permutation_order` | `D` (data)  | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_permutation_order: [u8; 19]` | yes |\n| 5 | `cp_len_extra_bits`    | `D` (data)  | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_len_extra_bits: [u8; 31]` | yes |\n| 6 | `cp_len_base`          | `D` (data)  | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_len_base: [u32; 31]` | yes |\n| 7 | `cp_dist_extra_bits`   | `D` (data)  | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_dist_extra_bits: [u8; 32]` | yes |\n| 8 | `cp_dist_base`         | `D` (data)  | `#[no_mangle] pub static mut cp_dist_base: [u32; 32]` | yes |\n\n**Missing from Rust `.so`: none.** The symbol diff is empty (verified by\n`check_symbols.sh`, which is also asserted by the integration test\n`symbols::c_and_rust_export_the_same_symbols`).\n\nSymbol *addresses* differ between the two libraries (link order is not part of\nthe ABI); the tests therefore compare symbol **contents**, not addresses.\nThe one place where this is observable is an out-of-bounds read past the end of\none of the tables — see the note at the bottom of `ERRORS.md`.\n\n## Internal (`static`) C functions — translated, deliberately **not** exported\n\nThese have internal linkage in C and so must *not* appear in `nm -D`.  All of\nthem exist in the Rust translation as private `fn`s:\n\n`cp_make_pixel_a`, `cp_make_pixel`, `cp_would_overflow`, `cp_ptr`,\n`cp_peak_bits`, `cp_consume_bits`, `cp_read_bits`, `cp_rev16`, `cp_build`,\n`cp_stored`, `cp_fixed`, `cp_decode`, `cp_dynamic`, `cp_block`.\n\nTypes `cp_pixel_t`, `cp_image_t`, `cp_state_t` are translated as `#[repr(C)]`\nstructs.  `cp_state_t`'s exact layout is *observable*: `cp_decode` reads\n`tree[-1]`, which aliases the struct member preceding `lit`/`dst`/`len`.  The\nRust translation static-asserts every field offset and `size_of` against the\nvalues gcc produces (`size_of == 2464`).\n\n## Undefined (imported) symbols\n\nThe C `.so` imports `__assert_fail`, `calloc`, `free`, `memcpy`, `memset`\n(plus the usual weak `__gmon_start__`, `__cxa_finalize`,\n`_ITM_*TMCloneTable`).  The Rust `.so` imports `__assert_fail`, `calloc`,\n`free` and open-codes `memcpy`/`memset` through `core::ptr` (compiler builtins),\nwhich is behaviourally identical.  There are **0 missing / unresolvable\nnon-libc undefined symbols** in the Rust `.so`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":6,"newStart":14,"newLines":13,"lines":[" ./check_symbols.sh"," ```"," ","+**Status: the symbol diff (C → Rust) is EMPTY.**  8 symbols exported by the C","+`.so`, all 8 exported by the Rust `.so` under the same names, all 8 resolvable","+through `dlsym`, all data symbols the same size.  Verified for the release","+cdylib, for `--no-default-features`, and for the debug cdylib","+(`./check_features.sh`).  Enforced by `tests/symbols.rs` (4 tests) as well as by","+`check_symbols.sh`.","+"," ## Exported (defined) symbols"," "," | # | symbol | C type | Rust definition | present in Rust `.so` |"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nmofuitje52jamizwztsmrult5xelgkhthoa2ocmmkn3vz23b2wa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass; the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte everywhere tested.\n\n## What was done\n\n**Fixes to the translation** (2, both required for correctness of observable behaviour):\n- `build.rs` + `src/lib.rs`: the live `assert()`s now pass the same absolute `__FILE__` that CMake compiles `lib.c` with, so the two libraries' abort messages on stderr are byte-identical rather than just \"both aborted\".\n- `Cargo.toml`: added `libloading`, `libc`, `flate2` as dev-dependencies.\n\nNo logic changes were needed — `cargo check` was already clean and the translation held up under ~32,000 adversarial cases.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (crate root): `SYMBOLS.md` (8 symbols, diff empty), `ERRORS.md` (16 rejection rows + 10 FFI-boundary rows), `CONFIGS.md` (39 configuration rows + 4 symbol checks). Scripts: `check_symbols.sh`, `check_features.sh`, `run_all.sh`.\n\n**Tests** (73, all via `libloading` against both `.so`s — never calling Rust directly): `tests/valid.rs` (38), `tests/errors.rs` (21), `tests/fuzz_sweep.rs` (10), `tests/symbols.rs` (4).\n\n## Harness problems worth knowing about\n\nThree things made naive differential testing produce false results, and each needed real infrastructure:\n\n1. **`cp_stored`'s `memcpy` has no `out_end` check** — it validates `LEN` only against the input, so a stored block writes up to 65 535 bytes past the caller's buffer. This smashed the test heap and surfaced as *fake* divergences (`munmap_chunk(): invalid pointer` vs `realloc(): invalid old size`). Fixed with `OUT_SLACK` = 64 KiB + 64, so the overrun is compared instead of corrupting the allocator. Row 39 now hammers it deliberately.\n2. **The C loops forever** on some corrupt dynamic headers — `cp_dynamic` writes `lens[n]` unbounded and can clobber its own loop counter `n`. 1 104 sweep cases hang; both libraries hang on exactly the same ones. Each case runs in a forked grandchild under a `setitimer` watchdog so a hang is a comparable outcome.\n3. **`SIGABRT` cost ~235 ms per case** here (core-dump handling), which made sweeps unusable. Catching the fatal signals in the grandchild took 800 cases from ~200 s to under 1 s.\n\n## Notable coverage\n\n- `cp_ptr`'s alignment assert (`lib.c:95`) is only reachable via `cp_peak_bits`'s final-word fold (`count += bits_left` instead of `+= 8*last_bytes`). I derived a 15-byte two-block stream for it; it hit on the first candidate.\n- `ERRORS.md` rows 8/11/13 are argued structurally unreachable, and a test asserts lines 104/124/126 never fire. Lines actually reached: 95, 115, 123, 125, 127, 154, 217.\n- The exported tables are writable, so they're the API's real \"enum\" surface — 1 200 poisoned-table cases plus targeted pokes reach rows 10 and 15.\n- The suite also passes against a **debug** cdylib (integer-overflow checks on), which rules out the translation being correct only because release mode wraps silently.\n\nTwo caveats I chose not to force agreement on, both documented rather than papered over: reads *past the end* of a global table (linker ordering differs and it's unconstrained UB — `cp_decode`'s assert fires first in practice), and `out == NULL` with a dereferencing stream under the debug profile only, where Rust's null check aborts where C takes `SIGSEGV`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":931,"cache_read_input_tokens":313512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":931,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b11a9639-5121-4054-9400-a5599ce5e3a1","uuid":"169f1337-cb1a-4307-babb-a39597697029","timestamp":"2026-09-05T11:27:27.177Z"}
